{"id": "EUVD-2026-86893", "enisaUuid": "391d66c0-d681-367a-b0ba-886677322d49", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nafs: Fix double-unmap of directory block\n\nFix afs_edit_dir_remove() to use a cleanup function to unmap the block\npointed to by afs_dir_iter::block if it's left pointing to something rather\nthan manually kunmapping the blocks.  Manually kunmapping without clearing\niter.blocks can result in a double-kunmap if afs_dir_find_block() is called\ntwice in a row (which would be the case if the block being modified is not\nfirst in the hash chain).", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d6c703e24da3d39067e3c75f4ac2f6001c2472f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b60f51e4ad0f6f940899788ccc2762db1e3b69e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3cfd3eb7d5be7787cc69530b423f788f14d084f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cgwc-p322-356w", "CVE-2026-97585"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "395ef01f-9782-3541-946a-0c7073402b12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "3b97c2fe-5c99-3bb9-a365-608684d36278", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5b5beebcf96d5e8a2fc79856c2ac1e93f82478e <9d6c703e24da3d39067e3c75f4ac2f6001c2472f"}, {"id": "6d2a5a34-518b-3f5f-9c1f-217a21f1e416", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "6dc2ded4-0b03-3e91-9a3c-f111ac2cbeee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7c56c53e-816f-38d3-ad8b-387bfb7bfe7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a5b5beebcf96d5e8a2fc79856c2ac1e93f82478e <e3cfd3eb7d5be7787cc69530b423f788f14d084f"}, {"id": "a03fa789-508b-3ed9-9acf-31176d124cad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"n